-- 40 small top-N scans of a table with order_columns: each opens its units once, reads the sort key of the rows that survive, and keeps its buffers small
-- label: 40 x `ORDER BY customer_id LIMIT 10..49`, `order_columns = 'customer_id'`, no btree on the column
-- ordered: no
